The [[☃ definition 2]] will pass through points $(1,h(1))$ and $(4,h(4))$.

$\begin{align}
\text{slope}&=\dfrac{\text{change in }y}{\text{change in }x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{h(4)-h(1)}{4-1}
\end{align}$

![Function h is graphed. The x-axis goes from negative 1 to 5. The graph consists of a curve. The curve starts in quadrant 2, moves upward to about (0, 16), moves downward through a point at (1, h of 1) and then a point at (4, h of 4), and ends in quadrant 4. A secant line connects the 2 points.](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/2ebff071978ab1b01531e1b7c549412c3da75a66)
